[ceiling] Wrong assumed print direction for this factory tool. Its documented common Y87.265 back lies on the bed after a −90° X rotation, building along machine −Y. The reported Z-normal bridge face is vertical in that pose. The actual-STL pose review in magnet-geometry.json/factory_gauges finds zero horizontal undersides above the bed.
alternatives: Printing in machine +Z requires support below the bridge and risks its registering faces. The specified flat-back pose puts the central rib, both feet and bridge directly on their common bed plane while preserving the 2.000 mm pole-setting step. No machine-frame geometry change is needed.
